## 6. Design Blocks

### 6.1 AND_4bit

The `AND_4bit` block performs a bitwise AND operation:

```text
Y[3:0] = A[3:0] AND B[3:0]
```

Example:

```text
A = 1010
B = 1101
Y = 1000
```

![4-bit AND Block](images/and_4bit.png)

### 6.2 OR_4bit

The `OR_4bit` block performs a bitwise OR operation:

```text
Y[3:0] = A[3:0] OR B[3:0]
```

Example:

```text
A = 1100
B = 0011
Y = 1111
```

![4-bit OR Block](images/or_4bit.png)

### 6.3 XOR_4bit

The `XOR_4bit` block performs a bitwise XOR operation:

```text
Y[3:0] = A[3:0] XOR B[3:0]
```

Example:

```text
A = 1001
B = 0011
Y = 1010
```

![4-bit XOR Block](images/xor_4bit.png)

### 6.4 ADD_4bit

The `ADD_4bit` block is a 4-bit Ripple Carry Adder built from four 1-bit Full Adders.

`FA0` processes bit 0, the least significant bit. `FA3` processes bit 3, the most significant bit. The carry-out of each stage is connected to the carry-in of the next stage:

```text
FA0.Cout -> FA1.Cin
FA1.Cout -> FA2.Cin
FA2.Cout -> FA3.Cin
```

The four individual sum bits are combined to form `SUM[3:0]`. The carry-out from `FA3` becomes the final `Cout`.

The initial `Cin` of `ADD_4bit` is set to `0` in the current ALU.

![4-bit Ripple Carry Adder](images/add_4bit.png)

### 6.5 Full Adder 1-bit

The 1-bit Full Adder receives three inputs and produces two outputs:

| Signal | Direction | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `A` | Input | First input bit |
| `B` | Input | Second input bit |
| `Cin` | Input | Carry-in |
| `Sum` | Output | Sum bit |
| `Cout` | Output | Carry-out |

The circuit is built using:

- 2 XOR gates
- 2 AND gates
- 1 OR gate

Its internal logic is:

```text
S1   = A XOR B
C1   = A AND B
Sum  = S1 XOR Cin
C2   = S1 AND Cin
Cout = C1 OR C2
```

![1-bit Full Adder](images/full_adder_1bit.png)

## 7. Hierarchical Design

The project uses a hierarchical and modular structure:

```text
Mini 4-bit ALU
|
|-- AND_4bit
|-- OR_4bit
|-- XOR_4bit
|
`-- ADD_4bit
    |
    |-- Full Adder 0
    |-- Full Adder 1
    |-- Full Adder 2
    `-- Full Adder 3
```

Dividing the ALU into smaller subcircuits made each function easier to build and test. It also allowed the same 1-bit Full Adder design to be reused four times inside `ADD_4bit`.

Each functional block was tested separately before being integrated into the complete ALU.

## 8. Verification

### 8.1 Test Strategy

Verification was performed in two stages:

1. Test the AND, OR, XOR, Full Adder, and Ripple Carry Adder blocks separately.
2. Integrate the blocks into the ALU and test all operations through `SEL[1:0]`.

The following operation mapping was checked during integration testing:

```text
SEL = 00 -> AND
SEL = 01 -> OR
SEL = 10 -> XOR
SEL = 11 -> ADD
```

The test cases include zero inputs, different bit patterns, and additions with and without carry-out.

### 8.2 Test Results

| Test | A | B | AND | OR | XOR | ADD | Cout |
|---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| 1 | `1010` | `1100` | `1000` | `1110` | `0110` | `0110` | `1` |
| 2 | `0000` | `0000` | `0000` | `0000` | `0000` | `0000` | `0` |
| 3 | `1010` | `0101` | `0000` | `1111` | `1111` | `1111` | `0` |
| 4 | `1111` | `0001` | `0001` | `1111` | `1110` | `0000` | `1` |
| 5 | `1111` | `1111` | `1111` | `1111` | `0000` | `1110` | `1` |

An additional integrated test used:

```text
A = 1011
B = 1101
```

| SEL | Operation | Y | Cout |
|:---:|---|:---:|:---:|
| `00` | AND | `1001` | Not used |
